{"content":"Fixed. The failure-reason preference in the per-check assembly (now `buildCheckLogSections`, extracted from `detectFailedChecks`) is:

```javascript
var reason = (jenkinsResult.reason && !jenkinsResult.skipped)
    ? jenkinsResult.reason
    : (ghResult.reason || jenkinsResult.reason || 'unknown fetch failure');
```

So when the `details_url` resolved to a Jenkins build target but the Jenkins fetch threw/came back empty, the md/full-log now report e.g. `log fetch failed: Jenkins log fetch failed: jenkins exploded` instead of the misleading `unsupported details_url shape: <jenkins-url>`. The `skipped: true` discriminator keeps the foreign-host case on the GitHub reason.

Regression test added: `a failed Jenkins fetch reports the Jenkins reason, not "unsupported details_url shape"` (fails on the old code, verified RED first). The two pre-existing tests for unconfigured-base-path and foreign-host Jenkins URLs still pin the GitHub-reason behavior there.
