Wait — new functions not in the baseline must be ≤ threshold 8 even with zero coverage? No — CRAP includes coverage; a fully covered function has CRAP = CC regardless. But the ratchet computes CRAP using the coverage from the run. A new function with CC 4 fully covered → CRAP 4 ≤ 8 fine. The gate flags NEW functions whose measured CRAP > 8. So tests matter.

Estimated CCs: fetchGithubJobLogsDetailed: try/catch + if = CC ~4. fetchGithubCheckRunLogsDetailed: ~4. fetchGithubCheckLogsDetailed: 5 branches → CC ~5, fully covered by dispatch tests. fetchGithubRunLogsDetailed after extraction: if(!runId), try, if(out) = ~4. runLogsFailureReason: if = 2.

